THIRD-PARTY CODE VENDORED IN THIS TREE

The three-way split above does NOT cover everything. These paths carry their
own licenses and their own copyright holders, and nothing here relicenses
them:

- tools/pyjkernel/          GPL-3.0. (c) Aurum. Full text in
                            tools/pyjkernel/LICENSE. Used by tools/arc_tool.py.
                            NOT MIT, despite the "tools/" line above.
- dc/third_party/sh4zam/    MIT. (c) 2025, 2026 Falco Girgis and SH4ZAM
                            Contributors. See dc/third_party/sh4zam/LICENSE
                            and dc/third_party/VENDORING.md. Vendored verbatim.
- include/PR/               Nintendo 64 SDK headers carrying a 1994 Silicon
                            Graphics, Inc. proprietary notice that forbids
                            redistribution. Required by the decompilation
                            (13,042 files include gbi.h) and inherited from
                            upstream ac-decomp, where they are equally
                            present. They are NOT CC0 and are NOT ours to
                            license. Listed here so the situation is disclosed
                            rather than implied.
- include/MSL_C/            Metrowerks Standard Library headers, plus Sun
                            Microsystems fdlibm under MSL_Common_Embedded/Math.
- include/dolphin/          GameCube SDK-shaped headers, community
                            reconstructed, no upstream notice.
- pc/lib/glad/              glad OpenGL loader generator output (public
                            domain / MIT per the generator).


What is and is not here, stated precisely:

- No disc image, ROM dump, or extracted asset file (textures, models, audio,
  archives) is contained in this repository, and none is licensed by either
  of the above. Building a playable image requires your own legally obtained
  copy of the game; its archives are read at build time and at runtime and
  are never redistributed here.

- src/ IS a decompilation: C source reconstructed from the retail game,
  including the data tables that source compiles. It is published by
  ACreTeam under CC0. Nintendo authored neither it nor its license and
  retains all rights in the original work. Nothing here is affiliated with,
  endorsed by, or sponsored by Nintendo or Sega.


